PS5 HDMI resolutions

1. The modes the bridge has a setup for, in their standard timings: 1080p60,
   1080p120, 2160p60 (CEA VICs 16/63/97), 1440p60 (VESA DMT) and on FLAVA3
   1440p120 (CVT-RB, high-bandwidth setup like 2160p60). Offered whenever the
   sink's limits allow them (highest refresh, max TMDS clock, a listed mode
   at that size or above), also when its EDID doesn't list them; the sink's
   own 1440p variants are dropped. 1080p60 is marked preferred, so a new
   display starts there; compositors remember a higher mode once picked.
2. FLAVA3 1440p sync safety net: both syncs get the standard shape and
   polarity of 2560x1440@60 (+hsync 32 px / 80 px back porch, -vsync with a
   33-line back porch); the bridge moves the picture by the pulse width when
   a polarity differs (-hsync: 32 px left, +vsync: 5 lines up).
3. Skip modes the sink accepts only as YCbCr 4:2:0 (sent labelled as RGB).
---

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
